WEBVTT

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.610
If your job is to catch me,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.160
then as a policewoman, it's also your job
to save lives. Am I right?

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:22.370
There's pretty much no one on this planet who
knows that it's set to explode right on schedule.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.750
I don't give a damn about what happens to these
assholes blowing each other away without a care,

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.880
but it'd be pretty sad if the people who weren't
like that just went "boom" all of a sudden.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.720
I want you to try and get as many civilians
as possible off the planet.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.850
What are you staying here for?

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.650
Coyotes won't betray their kin,
even if it costs them their lives!

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.070
There are some folks on this planet
who are still waiting for me.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.900
I've gotta go to them.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.700
I... l...

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.870
I'm no good at the romantic stuff.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.210
All right, girl, switch with me.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.970
All right!

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.370
Let's move!

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.180
Hokorimamire no bonnet

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.600
yubi de kyou o kizamu

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.060
Toori ame ga sugiru koro

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.900
ai no you ni kieta

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:17.150
Kokoro no naka nakusenu mono aru kara

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.240
Mienai tsubasa habatakase

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:30.500
Koredemo katto fuku kaze ni mukaiuchi

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:37.760
Yuruginai kimochi de tachimukatteku no sa, go!

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:44.680
Sunabokori mau yakusoku no basho e

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:50.650
Oretachi wa hashiritsuzukete yuku

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.820
Konya koso

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.320
Koete yaru

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:05.080
Ano saki made

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.210
This is the end of the line.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.840
I'm counting on you.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:25.810
Tell as many people you can 
the truth about the photonic bomb.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.430
See ya!

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:30.890
Mister...

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.980
When this is all over...

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.650
I'll be coming to catch you.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.400
I'll be waiting for ya.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.830
Okay! There's no time to lose.
We're heading out right away.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.840
Please wait up, Angelica!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.880
What's the situation?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.970
<i>We're currently investigating the whereabouts
of the two female detectives.</i>

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:08.350
Episode 11        Fading Memories

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:08.350
<i>We have also been informed that one of our own 
squad's vehicles assisted the two in their escape,</i>

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.180
<i>and we are presently seeking to verify that as well.</i>

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.140
April, Octo, Nove and Dece are currently heading
towards Godwing from Graceland's Philip Desert.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.820
<i>April, Octo, Nove and Dece are currently heading
towards Godwing from Graceland's Philip Desert.</i>

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:23.280
<i>January, March, June, July and August
are currently exploring the caves.</i>

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.370
<i>There have been not been any reports of
Gigabanks being found yet.</i>

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.990
<i>May is aboard this ship, awaiting the order to sortie.</i>

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.700
Well done.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.220
There's no time!

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:45.640
It's really... It's really going to explode!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:49.350
The photonic bomb is buried underground
not far from here!

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.770
"The one in satellite orbit aboard
the Jupiter was a fake.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:00.980
The real photonic bomb is already ticking down,
deep below the surface of this planet.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:03.900
We are in danger and must evacuate quickly."

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.120
You think I'm just going to believe
such nonsense at face value?

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.660
It is the truth, regardless.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.830
Indeed.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.210
Well, it is a rather interesting story, but...

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.000
There is also a certain rumor I heard,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.420
about a certain Federal inspector who
has Presidential authorizations.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.550
It is a pleasure to meet you.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.930
I don't know what your aim is,

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.640
but we are the Graceland Liberation Forces,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.180
and we do not take orders from any
of the Federation's hounds!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.680
Now leave.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.350
Angelica...

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:41.320
The Federation forces have already
begun their evacuation,

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:45.450
and your Liberation Forces should have also
obtained that information by now!

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:51.700
That's precisely why you let us into this base,
knowing that we were with the Federation!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.330
In order to know the truth...

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.670
There's no time to lose!

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.500
Please!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.180
Where's the next base?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.050
Well... Right here!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.680
Okay, let's go.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.310
We'll do everything we can.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.730
Oh, man.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.440
We've got under seven hours now.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.480
Katana!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.230
There! There's a tunnel on the
other side of that rock.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.820
For real?!

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.370
<i>Mister...</i>

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.490
<i>We're waiting for you.</i>

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.750
Angelica?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:45.590
Do you think those soldiers we
saw earlier believed us?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.880
Hard to say.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.760
If they'd just use their network
to contact the other bases...

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.060
That would be the best case scenario.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.270
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.230
Chelsea?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.020
Yes?

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:05.070
You once asked me what motivated
me to pursue Mister.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.610
Do you still want to know'?

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.320
You don't mind?

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.200
I was still 22, fresh out of the police academy.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.740
At the time, he was a wanted man
because of a certain event.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:21.370
That was eight years ago... 2033.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.590
Oh! The Diamondhead Incident!

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:25.170
That's correct!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.720
That was when I first encountered Mister.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.180
The very first case...

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.480
But I was new to the force and they
just had me doing traffic control.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.110
When there was a lot of congestion, all the honking
would come down on you like a ton of bricks.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.530
It was one hot day.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.440
The sun was beating down so strongly...

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.740
I was frantic trying to direct traffic.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.410
And then...

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.200
everything went quiet, as if there had
never been any of the previous racket.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.250
It was like time had hiccupped.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:06.500
I slowly started to make out something
shining in the distance.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.220
It took me a moment to register that it was a wave.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.270
Everyone, please escape to higher ground!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.690
Hurry!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.870
He was atop the wave.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:49.050
He passed by me way up in the air,

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:53.010
smiling like a boy, like he was having fun
and was as pleased as could be.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.390
What are you doing? C'mon!

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.100
I felt as though I was dreaming.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:07.440
After that, I thoroughly investigated this man,

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.820
this "Mister."

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.110
Then four years ago, there was another event,

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.530
which led to my appointment as an
investigator specializing in Mister.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.570
That was in 2037.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.200
The Firegate Incident!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.120
Correct!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.790
That attempt to involve the president in a scandal...

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:29.170
I found out about the plot just by chance
while pursuing Mister.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:31.420
And that led to the matter being resolved.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:36.340
It was all done in an attempt to give an edge to the
presidential candidate backed by the Guild, right?

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.800
And that's why you now have special
presidential authorization.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.100
Perhaps...

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.430
Yes?

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.930
Never mind.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:57.740
Perhaps I've been lying to myself ever since
that first time I saw him on Diamondhead.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:06.160
Perhaps I was suppressing my true feelings
by chasing Mister, the criminal.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:10.920
Nilson...

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.550
Are you going?

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.630
Yes, I'm going to settle the score.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.260
With Mister?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.930
No, with myself.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.270
I see.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.650
We have received word from the squad
exploring the caves.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:32.070
Mister has been located at Godwing, point 03.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.690
We will now commence attack.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.490
Very well.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.570
Don't you die now.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:42.660
When you're old, the more people around,
the better. It's less lonesome that way.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.040
Nilson?

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.120
What is it?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.750
I wonder if the way I've been living has been right?

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.330
You are not in the wrong!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.710
You are still you, no matter where you go.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.700
Mister...

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.300
Mister!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.100
Hey!

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.260
Mister!

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.100
Sorry I'm late.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.430
Boss, this thing is...

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:36.400
Yeah, the effects of the war probably caused
the underground water veins to go haywire.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.650
What do we do? We've only got
about three hours left.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:41.440
Mister?

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:42.820
There's no time to spare.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:48.450
If we retreat before checking out his treasure,
Bruce will only feel shut out, right?

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.080
Franca...

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.750
Sorry to keep you waiting so long.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:59.090
Shall we go see your old man?

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.760
Let's go, Mister.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.800
Let's go.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.430
Papa's waiting.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:12.730
Right.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:16.860
Well, I'd like to say let's all get a move on, but...

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:21.110
I guess you had yourself a flashy gunfight with the
Guild gals on the way over here, didn't ya?

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.950
I'll take care of things here. You two get going.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:26.530
You're pretty cool, man.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.620
You know it.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:30.120
But we're not paying ya back for it.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.160
As the Coyotes say,

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.420
"Whatever you borrow, don't give back,
even if it means dying!"

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.090
Now get going!

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:39.920
Right!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.460
Oh... Katana!

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.210
Huh?

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.510
Thanks!

00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.010
Hurry up, Franca!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.430
Okay!

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:56.060
Good luck, you two.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.190
Friggin' asshole...

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.900
Can't you do something?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.400
With this craft...

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.700
there ain't a thing I can do!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.990
The button goes "blip"!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.920
There's one present for Mother.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.550
We'll head straight on to Godwing.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:26.630
Roger!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.350
We alive?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:40.520
This is a damn rough trip for my comeback tour.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.480
We're not far from the Coyote.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:45.900
How much time left?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.740
Don't ask.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.370
This way. Run!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.700
For cryin' out loud, I don't get any breaks!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.870
Gigabanks starts to "reshuffle" itself
upon final authentication,

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.540
and once you enter any of its parts, that's that.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.880
It turns into a maze from which you'll
never be able to escape.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.590
Right?

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.430
We're going to take the same route that Bruce did.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.600
So it's started...

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.770
It has here too!

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.040
Mister!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.420
I'm all right.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.100
You all right?

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.140
Yeah...

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.730
Well, the first round's over.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.610
We've got thirty minutes until the next reshuffling.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.520
Can you manage it?

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.190
Of course!
Can you manage it?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:07.480
Of course!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.610
Okay, this way.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.160
Queen to Bishop Six.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.830
Knight takes Queen.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.300
Bishop taking Seven.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.220
Check!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.930
Bingo.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.850
Amazing...

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.770
That's the center ball, the heart of Gigabanks.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:50.570
Papa planted a bomb in there and used the
security system itself to his own advantage.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.780
Yeah...

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.380
Gigabanks...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.570
That lonely feeling after the party has ended...

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:20.030
Ten billion soaked space dollars...

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.160
We came all this way,

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.620
but it doesn't look like we'll have
the time to take this all back.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:29.290
Then I'll just take this as a keepsake.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.130
Franca!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.620
Papa?!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.100
Me too.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.650
I...

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.740
I love you too, Papa!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.950
Not that way! More to the north!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.710
What are you talking about?!

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.130
We can't just cruise on in to Godwing like this!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:38.380
Those Guild bastards probably expect us
and are lying in wait right now.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.300
You're probably right,

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:42.880
but if we can't get the Coyote right up
alongside Gigabanks,

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.350
it won't be possible to get the money out in time!

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:46.760
It's all right!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:48.850
Leave it to me!

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:51.180
I've got a good idea!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.810
Mother...

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.570
We were waiting for you.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:00.240
Where is January's group?

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:01.950
They went in just a moment ago.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.400
I'll show you the way.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:11.330
Bullets are so much simpler than a knife.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.080
You can't interfere!

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.880
January, August...

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:26.930
Mother?

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.600
The two of you have done well.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.560
Where is June?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.270
Over there, she's hogging all the fun to herself.

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:37.900
Mother?

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:40.940
Coyote...

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:45.490
Here and now I shall obliterate
all that can perturb me.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:49.330
Come, let us start the final party!

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.750
Mister!

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:09.140
Mister!

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.870
Next time
Final Installment

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:42.960
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru</i>

00:22:43.050 --> 00:22:53.470
<i>shizuku doko kara kuru no</i>

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:58.730
<i>Oshiete...</i>

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:04.360
<i>Makimodosenai</i>

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:11.070
<i>jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:18.040
<i>munagura tsukanda</i>

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:22.630
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae</i>

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.210
<i>usuragu kioku ni</i>

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>teikou suru keredo</i>

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:36.810
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru</i>

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:43.270
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de</i>

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:51.780
<i>tatta hitotsu shinjirareru</i>

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:58.160
<i>Koe o karasete naita</i>

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:01.460
<i>Koko e kite</i>

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.790
<i>Soba ni ite</i>

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:09.130
<i>Nee</i>
